    "abstract": "Parts breakdown of the forward cargo door latching installation, showing the eight latch pin housings, the splice plate in both bushing standards and the harness retention hardware on the latch beam.",
    "sections": {
      "purpose": "This figure gives the parts breakdown of the forward cargo door latching installation, from the latch beam outward to the eight latch pin housings and the retention hardware.",
      "figure_note": "Sheet 1 shows the latch beam with the door open, viewed from inside the compartment; sheet 2 shows the pre-modification harness routing. Items 20 and 20A are the two latch pin housing sets. Each is a matched group of bushing, latch pin and retention ring, and each is supplied complete. The two sets are NOT INTERCHANGEABLE in either direction: the housing bore is re-machined to a larger diameter when the self-lubricating liner is installed, so the greased bronze bushing of item 20 is loose in an enlarged bore and the liner bushing of item 20A will not enter a standard bore. Do not order a single component against either set as a substitution for the other, and do not read the earlier note that allowed a bushing to be ordered on its own; it is deleted with this issue. Establish the housing bore standard from the aircraft configuration record before ordering."
    },
